The best interval we can use (the interval whose points are given that's closest to $x=7$) is the interval between $x=6$ and $x=7$. Let's find the average rate of change between those points.

$\begin{align}
f'(7)&\approx\dfrac{f(7)-f(6)}{7-6}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{53-35}{1}
\\\\
&=18
\end{align}$
